        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. Verizon North Inc. (North Central Region) agrees to make available a Living Benefit Rider (LBR) to employees and their spouses who are presently enrolled in Group Universal Life (GUL) Insurance.",
            "block_bbox": [
                183,
                451,
                1029,
                540
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    183.0,
                    451.0
                ],
                [
                    1029.0,
                    451.0
                ],
                [
                    1029.0,
                    540.0
                ],
                [
                    183.0,
                    540.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. The Company and the Union recognize that long term care will continue to be the most likely catastrophic illness risk facing employees. As a result of these concerns and for these reasons, the LBR option to GUL is established to provide protection against the financial ravages of declining health.",
            "block_bbox": [
                179,
                563,
                1057,
                706
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    179.0,
                    563.0
                ],
                [
                    1057.0,
                    563.0
                ],
                [
                    1057.0,
                    706.0
                ],
                [
                    179.0,
                    706.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. The LBR provides a benefit equal to 2% of the face value of the policy (excluding any cash value amounts) per month for a period up to 25 months. In effect, the LBR can pay out a maximum of 50% of the face value of the policy (25 months × 2%). The maximum potential benefit is $10,000 per month with a minimum potential monthly benefit of $400.",
            "block_bbox": [
                179,
                729,
                1046,
                872
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    179.0,
                    729.0
                ],
                [
                    1046.0,
                    729.0
                ],
                [
                    1046.0,
                    872.0
                ],
                [
                    179.0,
                    872.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. Eligibility for the benefit shall be based on the following conditions:",
            "block_bbox": [
                178,
                895,
                983,
                926
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 8,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    178.0,
                    895.0
                ],
                [
                    983.0,
                    895.0
                ],
                [
                    983.0,
                    926.0
                ],
                [
                    178.0,
                    926.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A. Employees or spouses must be continuously unable to care for themselves in a minimum of three activities of daily living for at least six months. Activities of daily living are defined as eating, getting around, transferring, toileting, bathing, and dressing.",
            "block_bbox": [
                258,
                950,
                1039,
                1066
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 9,
            "group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    258.0,
                    950.0
                ],
                [
                    1039.0,
                    950.0
                ],
                [
                    1039.0,
                    1066.0
                ],
                [
                    258.0,
                    1066.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "B. Employees or spouses must submit written medical evidence that shows the inability to perform the activities of daily living.",
            "block_bbox": [
                261,
                1087,
                1017,
                1148
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 9,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    261.0,
                    1087.0
                ],
                [
                    1017.0,
                    1087.0
                ],
                [
                    1017.0,
                    1148.0
                ],
                [
                    261.0,
                    1148.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "C. The condition causing the inability to care for oneself cannot be a condition for which the individual received medical care or treatment during the six months immediately before LBR coverage became effective (pre-existing condition clause).",
            "block_bbox": [
                259,
                1170,
                1061,
                1284
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 11,
            "group_id": 10,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    259.0,
